n. Some propose a derivation from reconstructed Gothic *𐌱𐌰𐍅𐌹𐌸𐌰 (*bawiþa), presumably from 𐌱𐌰𐌿𐌰𐌽 (bauan). Despite the surface sound similarity, a derivation from Arabic بَيْت (bayt, “house”) is unlikely."},{"parola":"bega","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"quarrel, dispute","termine_origine":"*𐌱𐌴𐌲𐌰","catena":[{"codice":"got","nome":"Gothic","termine":"*𐌱𐌴𐌲𐌰","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*bēganą","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Gothic *𐌱𐌴𐌲𐌰 (*bēga, “quarrel”), ultimately from the root of Proto-Germanic *bēganą."},{"parola":"brace","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably; perhaps","significato":"ember(s)","termine_origine":"*𐌱𐍂𐌰𐍃𐌰","catena":[{"codice":"got","nome":"Gothic","termine":"*𐌱𐍂𐌰𐍃𐌰","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*brasō","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*bʰres-","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Perhaps from Gothic *𐌱𐍂𐌰𐍃𐌰 (*brasa, “glowing coal”), from Proto-Germanic *brasō (“gleed, crackling coal”), from Proto-Indo-European *bʰres- (“to crack, break, burst”). Cognate with French braise (“embers”), Swedish brasa (“to roast”), Icelandic brasa (“to harden by fire”). Most probably cognate to S"},{"parola":"buzzurro","pos":"adj|noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Unknown; Possibly","significato":"rude, impolite, coarse","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"got","nome":"Gothic","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"lng","nome":"Lombardic","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"lng","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Unknown, possibly of Gothic or Lombardic origin."},{"parola":"randa","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"